{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"landpoor-doggoned-alleycat","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Why\nClosing satiated-unrideable-tapeworm (Gerrit 1809, merged 42cd70b889) left three residual sub-clauses that are test/reporting hardening, not behavior gaps — all behavior is merged, tested observable-behaviour-style, and CI-green. This ticket carries the remainder so the parent could close honestly.\n\n## Scope (from the parent's AC1-AC3 residuals; full tables in the parent's close-out comment)\n1. AC1 residual: add call-count/monkeypatch assertions on the shared confirmation reduce path so a future regression that bypasses the shared seam (printing per-verb again) is caught structurally, not just per-verb by exact-line tests.\n2. AC2 residual: ship the verb inventory table (no-op-capable vs always-writes) as generated or hand-maintained documentation (docs/cli-reference or a test-enforced table), so the no-op contract is enumerable.\n3. AC3 residual: record the per-verb old→new confirmation-line mapping (the parent's comment has the full table) in docs or the test suite as golden data.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Reduce-path structural assertion exists (call-count or seam-spy) covering at least create/link/transition.\n- [ ] Verb inventory (no-op-capable vs always-writes) lives in a durable, reviewable location and a test fails when a verb is added without classification.\n- [ ] Old→new mapping table recorded in docs or golden test data.\n- [ ] make lint / make typecheck clean; lands via Gerrit.","id":"0c00-0649-32da-41a5","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Tapeworm follow-up: reduce-path structural tests + verb no-op inventory + confirmation-line mapping record"},"env_i